                    <occupation>Clerk and Antiquary</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> George Vanderzee, side clerk, Kings Remembrancer's office, Exchequer,
                            (La2w list 1800) became fellow of Society of Antiquaries 14.1.1796 of 2
                            Brick Court, Middle Temple, married 24.5.1798 St Mary Newington Mary daughter
                            of the late G D Hammond Esq of Lawling Hall, Essex. George Vanderzee buried
                            10.4.1837 age 71 St Pancras will PCC 1837. His family of Billericay
                            Essex, various PCC wills, James V attorney Billericay, Daniel V London
                            merchant bankrupt 1803, John V master in Chancery 1793 etc. </p>
                    </note>
